From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:18:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: program the VoW band of a new interface
 on success

Commit 6b7b98627bcc ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: HW ATF support for mt7986+")
added the mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band() call at the single exit of
mt7915_add_interface(). Commit c52a151151c1 ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind
state on add_interface failure") then gave the success path its own
early return, so the group-to-band mapping is now only sent when adding
the interface fails, and never for an interface that was actually added.

Send it on the success path only.

Fixes: c52a151151c1 ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind state on add_interface failure")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/main.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/main.c b/mt7915/main.c
index d70a9c9e..8adbf480 100644
--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -279,6 +279,9 @@ static int mt7915_add_interface(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
+	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
+		mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif);
+
 	return 0;
 
 err:
@@ -290,9 +293,6 @@ out:
 		phy->monitor_vif = NULL;
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
-	if (!is_mt7915(&dev->mt76))
-		mt7915_mcu_set_vow_band(dev, mvif);
-
 	return ret;
 }
 
